    {
      "text": "seek, and ye shall find, Matt. 7:7 (Luke 11:9; 3 Ne. 14:7). narrow is the way … few there be that find it, Matt. 7:14 (3 Ne. 27:33). I have not found so great faith, Matt. 8:10 (Luke 7:9). He that findeth his life shall lose it, Matt. 10:39. house … when he is come, he findeth it empty, Matt. 12:44 (Luke 11:25). found one pearl of great price, Matt. 13:46. lose his life for my sake shall find it, Matt. 16:25. he find it … rejoiceth more of that sheep, Matt. 18:13. servant, whom his lord when he cometh shall find so doing, Matt. 24:46 (Luke 12:43). cometh unto the disciples, and findeth them asleep, Matt. 26:40 (Mark 14:37; Luke 22:45). eat … with unwashen, hands, they found fault, Mark 7:2. Lest coming suddenly he find you sleeping, Mark 13:36. Ye shall find the babe wrapped in swaddling, Luke 2:12. found Mary, and Joseph, and the babe, Luke 2:16. they found him in the temple, Luke 2:46. go after that which is lost, until he find it, Luke 15:4. this my son … was lost, and is found, Luke 15:24 (15:32). Son of man cometh, shall he find faith on the earth, Luke 18:8. I find no fault in this man, Luke 23:4 (John 18:38). found the stone rolled away from the sepulchre, Luke 24:2. We have found the Messias, John 1:41. We have found him, of whom Moses … did write, John 1:45. shall seek me, and shall not find me, John 7:34 (7:36). haply they might feel after him, and find him, Acts 17:27. Enoch … was not found, Heb. 11:5. shall men seek death, and shall not find it, Rev. 9:6. whosoever was not found written in the book, Rev. 20:15.",
